<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Al-Jawf (Yemen)</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Wadi al-Jawf</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Al-Jawf is a region of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a>, a broad desert valley north-east of Sanaa and north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marib">Marib</a>, now a governorate. In the 1st millennium BCE it held the city-states of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-main">Kingdom of Ma'in</a>, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qarnawu">Qarnawu</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baraqish">Yathill</a> (Baraqish), which grew rich on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/incense">incense</a> trade. Many of their ruined temples and city walls still stand.</p></div>
